# LaunchDek Standards

Cross-cutting quality standards. See also: `launchdek-project.mdc` (architecture), `launchdek-compliance.mdc` (pre-ship gate), `wordpress-php.mdc` (PHP/REST), `admin-assets.mdc` (JS/CSS).

## Coding Standards

- **PHP**: WordPress PHP Coding Standards — spacing, arrays, docblocks where useful, clear naming.
- **JS**: Vanilla admin JS with `fetch` + `launchdekAdmin` REST helpers; no frameworks unless justified.
- **CSS**: Scope styles to `.launchdek-*` selectors; avoid bleeding into wp-admin or themes.
- **HTML**: Semantic markup, accessible labels, buttons, headings.
- Never output inline CSS/JS unless there is a good reason.
- Keep lines and functions readable rather than clever.

## I18N

- All user-facing strings must be translatable via `LAUNCHDEK_TEXT_DOMAIN`.
- Use `__()`, `_e()`, `esc_html__()`, `esc_attr__()`, etc. appropriately.
- REST error messages returned to admin UI must also be translatable.

## Accessibility

- Every settings field must have a label.
- Use `<button>` elements for actions, not clickable divs.
- Respect keyboard navigation and focus states.
- Modals use `[hidden]` attribute; ensure focus trap where appropriate.

## Admin UX

- Add notices sparingly; use `.launchdek-notice-area` + WordPress core `.notice` / `.notice-error` / `.notice-success` (via JS `notice()` helper) for inline feedback.
- Load plugin-screen assets only via `is_plugin_screen()`.
- Features must respect the global `enabled` kill switch.
- Settings page uses WordPress Settings API (platform toggles, credential vault, exclude-options list, client panel layout picker + custom panel title, webhooks, role-permission matrix, onboarding preview button); all other pages use REST-driven JS UI.
- Shared modals (`launchdek-onboarding-modal.php`, `launchdek-template-picker-modal.php`, `launchdek-confirm-modal.php`) are thin partials included via `require` — do not duplicate markup across pages. Built-in template grid and vault live on the Checklists **Templates** tab (default; unified nav tabs, not a separate admin menu). Template/vault cards use **Use Checklist** to clone and open the builder; custom checklists are picked from the **My Checklists** dropdown only. **Start Blank** lives in the builder actions row. Auto-capture is an inline tab panel, not a modal. Confirm modal (`openConfirmModal()`) replaces browser `confirm()` for destructive actions (e.g. permanent run delete). Automation validation uses inline notices (`runNotice()`), not `alert()`.
- Modal close/dismiss: hide with `[hidden]` immediately; persist onboarding dismissal via REST in the background (do not block UI on network).
- Onboarding wizard auto-opens only on the dashboard (`data-launchdek-page="dashboard"` + `onboarding.show`); Settings includes the modal for **Show onboarding wizard** preview but does not auto-open after save. `?onboarding=1` still forces open on any screen with the modal partial.

## Performance

- Load code only where needed.
- Avoid expensive queries on every request; repositories should use indexed columns.
- Remote API calls only on user action, checklist execution, connection tests, scheduled drift cron, client panel snapshot sync after hub-side run advances (`sync_run()` → `push_run( $id, false, false )`, no bundle reinstall), initial push / manual **Refresh Client Panel** (`push_run` with `$sync_bundle = true`), site save/test bundle deploy, or auto-capture sessions — never on every admin page load except Sites page background stale-connection refresh (30-minute threshold) and on-demand site run history (`GET /sites/{id}/runs` when a site row is expanded). Client step toggles do not trigger hub→client re-sync; hub returns `snapshot` for local apply.
- Client panel assets (`wp_enqueue_media()`, panel JS/CSS) load only on remote wp-admin when an active run snapshot exists — not on every admin request.
- Dashboard stats, connection ticker, live log feed, and Quick Launch Bar picker options use `LAUNCHDEK_Dashboard_Cache` (`launchdek_dashboard_cache`, non-autoload); preloaded in PHP/`launchdekAdmin.dashboard` on dashboard load (Quick Launch selects also render server-side — no REST wait on first paint); cache invalidated on underlying data changes. Checklists page preloads custom checklist summaries via `launchdekAdmin.customChecklists` (`LAUNCHDEK_Checklist_Repository::summary_list()`); JS deduplicates picker/vault fetches through `fetchCustomChecklistSummaries()`. Builder preview loads client panel CSS (`launchdek-client-admin-preview`) on the Checklists screen only. Activity Logs page fetches via REST only when opened/filtered.
- Avoid autoloading large options.

## Privacy & External Communication

- No telemetry or undisclosed tracking.
- **Allowed outbound**: remote site REST calls (Application Passwords), client panel mu-plugin deploy/sync (user-initiated via site connect or push), webhook notifications (Slack/Discord/Teams — user-configured URLs only), integration adapter pushes (user-initiated).
- Webhook URLs and notification events are opt-in via Settings (`run_started`, `run_completed`, `run_failed`, `step_failed`, `drift_detected`, `client_step_completed`, `client_note_added`).
- Credential vault encrypts app passwords at rest when `encrypt_credentials` is enabled.
- Document any new external integration or client panel behavior in `readme.txt`.
- **Telemetry Sync Mapping Rules** on the Integrations page are user-configured field mappings for connector sync — not undisclosed tracking or outbound telemetry.

## Uninstall & Lifecycle

- **Activate**: seed settings, install DB tables, register caps, schedule drift cron, redirect to dashboard onboarding (`?onboarding=1`).
- **Deactivate**: clear activation redirect transient, unschedule drift cron.
- **Delete**: `uninstall.php` drops all tables, removes options (`launchdek_settings`, `launchdek_version`, `launchdek_db_version`, `launchdek_templates_seeded`, `launchdek_dashboard_cache`), unregisters capabilities.
- If adding new options or tables, update `uninstall.php` and `LAUNCHDEK_Installer::uninstall()`.

## Release

- Include `readme.txt` with changelog.
- Include license headers and `LAUNCHDEK_VERSION` in plugin header.
- Bump `LAUNCHDEK_Installer::DB_VERSION` when schema changes; add a `migrate_from_previous()` step for upgrades.
- New built-in template JSON files need no migration — `LAUNCHDEK_Templates::sync_builtin()` inserts missing slugs on init.
